WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.462
Never begin an analysis without first checking what actually loaded.

00:00:04.462 --> 00:00:08.417
The head function lets us inspect the first few rows.

00:00:08.417 --> 00:00:11.617
Shape tells us the number of rows and columns.

00:00:11.617 --> 00:00:20.032
The columns attribute shows the available column names, and sample lets us inspect a few records from different parts of

00:00:20.032 --> 00:00:23.917
the table. These simple checks can reveal problems immediately.

00:00:23.917 --> 00:00:27.457
Maybe the file has far fewer rows than expected.

00:00:27.457 --> 00:00:31.122
Maybe a column name contains an unexpected space.

00:00:31.122 --> 00:00:35.927
Maybe the values do not look like the data described in the documentation.

00:00:35.927 --> 00:00:41.352
A good habit is to record the row count before and after major cleaning steps.

00:00:41.352 --> 00:00:47.010
Unexpected changes in row count are often an early warning that something went wrong.
